HST Office on Windows: no registry key under LibreOffice's name, no LibreOffice publisher text.

The MSI wrote HKLM\Software\LibreOffice\Layers\URE\1 (a value LibreOffice writes too, so the last
installer owned it and an uninstall deleted it), Software\LibreOffice\Layers\HST Office\1.0,
Software\LibreOffice\Layers\Basis\1.0, Software\LibreOffice\HST Office\1.0 and
HKCR\Software\LibreOffice\HST Office. The scp2 items of a legacy uninstall key (Uninstall\HST
Office 1.0) named "The Document Foundation for the LibreOffice Community" as publisher and
libreoffice.org as help, about and update links; the MSI build does not emit that key (Programs
and Features uses the ARP properties), but the items should not name the other suite either.

- These keys are under Software\HASON TECH\ (%MANUFACTURER) now.
- Those uninstall items name HASON TECH and the same hasontech.vn link as the MSI's ARP
  properties.
- The MigrateInstallPath custom action is unchanged: it finds HST Office's install folder under
  Software\HASON TECH\HST Office\1.0\<UpgradeCode> first, and still reads the old
  Software\LibreOffice\Layers\HST Office key that beta 1-4 wrote, so their folder is kept.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

